Floyd-Warshall finds the shortest distance from every node to every other node.

class Solution {

    public void floydWarshall(int[][] dist) {.        // int[][] Because we need distance between every pair.

        int n = dist.length;

        for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {                // Intermediate node

            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {             // Source node

                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {         // Destination node

                    if (dist[i][k] != Integer.MAX_VALUE &&
                        dist[k][j] != Integer.MAX_VALUE) {

                        dist[i][j] = Math.min(
                            dist[i][j],
                            dist[i][k] + dist[k][j]
                        );
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}



//"Floyd-Warshall is an all-pairs shortest-path algorithm. 
// I maintain a 2D distance matrix where dist[i][j] represents the shortest known distance from i to j. 
// Then, for every node k, I consider it as an intermediate node and check whether going from i to k and then k to j is shorter than the current direct distance from i to j.
//  The update formula is dist[i][j] = min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j]). 
// The time complexity is O(V³), and it supports negative edge weights.
//  A negative diagonal value after the algorithm indicates a negative cycle."